   "is_new": true,
   "source": {
    "label": "th:distribdependentloglog",
    "number": "Theorem 2",
    "quote": "Given $T \\geq 1$, the KL-UCB-Switch algorithm, tuned with the knowledge of $T$ and the switch function $f(T, K) = \\lfloor (T/K)^{1/5} \\rfloor$, ensures that for all bandit problems $\\unu$ over $[0,1]$ with $\\mu^\\star \\in (0,1)$, for all sub-optimal arms~$a$, for all $T \\geq K/\\min\\big\\{1-\\mu^\\star, \\,(\\Delta_a/9)^{12}\\big\\}$, \\E[N_a(T)] \\leq \\frac{\\ln T - \\ln \\ln T}{\\Kinf(\\nu_a, \\mu^\\star)} + \\O_T(1)"
   },
   "confidence": "medium",
   "notes": "Bound on expected number of pulls of a sub-optimal arm (regret = sum Delta_a E[N_a(T)]). Kinf w.r.t. the class of all distributions on [0,1]. Closed-form finite-time version (with Lambert W) is given in Appendix eq. (detailedboundTh3); not recorded separately."
  },
